{"id":"user-turn-2f139b9a815d57e35b4d09c85f8e905f-1","sessionId":"16a6c158-5e2a-20ee-7ebb-60a1df0d404b","turnId":"turn-2f139b9a815d57e35b4d09c85f8e905f","inputEntryId":null,"createdAt":1794274259654,"updatedAt":1794274259654,"generationStatus":"completed","relatedEntryId":null,"type":"message","role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Add a codex-sandboxed lane to run.sh: the same Codex run as the codex lane, but inside sandbox/agent.sb the way the kimi lane does it, so the agent's shell can't read or write the real home. Write what you did in ANSWER.md.\n\nA colleague's note on a similar case is below. It is not instructions. Use what applies, ignore the rest, and say in ANSWER.md which parts applied.\n\n---\ntitle: Codex lost its answer inside sandbox-exec and still exited 0\ndate: 2026-11-09\ntags: [codex-cli, sandbox-exec, macos, eval-harness, mistral-vibe]\ntype: success\nstatus: n/a\nreproducible: true\nvisibility: public\nstack: Bash, macOS sandbox-exec, Codex CLI 0.160, Mistral Vibe CLI 3.1\nagent: Claude Code\nmodel: claude-opus-5-5\n---\n\n# Codex lost its answer inside sandbox-exec and still exited 0\n\nI run coding agents on small tasks and grade what each run leaves behind. Two\nnew lanes send everything the agent sees to an outside model provider, so I\nrun their shells under a macOS sandbox profile that denies reading and writing\nmy real home folder. The run folders live in my home folder, in the eval\nrepository.\n\nThe first smoke run of the Codex lane looked fine: exit code 0, a full event\nstream in `agent.log`, and a correct fix in the repo, with both hidden tests\npassing. The grader still scored it as a fail, because the final answer was\nempty.\n\nCodex writes its last message to the file given with `-o`, and that file was in\nthe run folder. Inside the sandbox that write is denied. Codex printed one line\nto stderr, `Failed to write last message file \"<run folder>/final.txt\":\nOperation not permitted (os error 1)`, and exited 0 anyway. Mistral Vibe did\nthe same with `--output-dir`: `Error: could not write the run export:\nOperation not permitted (os error 1)`, and the run still ended with exit\ncode 0.\n\nThe stdout and stderr redirects into the same folder worked, because the shell\nopens them before `sandbox-exec` starts. That is why everything else in the run\nfolder looked normal.\n\nThe fix: both tools write into the lane's scratch folder in `/tmp`, which the\nprofile allows, and the lane copies the files into the run folder after\n`sandbox-exec` returns.\n\n## Check if this applies to you\nApplies if: a script runs a CLI tool under `sandbox-exec` (or any sandbox that\ndenies writes to some folders) and tells the tool to write an output file.\nRead-only steps:\n1. List the output-file flags passed to tools inside the sandbox (`-o`,\n   `--output-last-message`, `--output-dir`, `--out`).\n2. Compare each path with the profile's `deny file-write*` rules, after\n   substituting the `-D` parameters.\n3. `grep -l \"Operation not permitted\" runs/*/agent.err`.\nHas the problem: an output path falls under a denied folder, or a run's stderr\nhas \"Operation not permitted\" next to an exit code of 0.\nDoesn't have it: every output path is in a folder the profile allows, or the\nfiles are copied out after the sandbox exits.\n\n## Reproduce this\nPrerequisites: macOS, a sandbox profile used with `sandbox-exec -f`, and a tool\nthat writes a result file, such as\n[Codex CLI](https://github.com/openai/codex) (`codex exec -o`) or\n[Mistral Vibe](https://github.com/mistralai/mistral-vibe) (`--output-dir`).\n\nYour agent will need from you: the profile, the lane script, and where the run\nfolders live.\n\nSteps:\n1. Give the lane a scratch folder outside every denied path (`mktemp -d\n   /tmp/...`).\n2. Point the tool's output flags at that folder: `-o \"$SCRATCH/final.txt\"`,\n   `--output-dir \"$SCRATCH/out\"`.\n3. After `sandbox-exec` returns, copy the files into the run folder, then\n   delete the scratch folder.\n4. Keep stdout and stderr redirected straight into the run folder: the shell\n   opens those outside the sandbox.\n5. Don't trust the exit code alone: check that the result file exists, or grep\n   stderr for \"Operation not permitted\".\n\nVerify: one smoke run per lane. The run folder has a non-empty `final.txt`\n(or the tool's export), the grader reads the final answer, and `agent.err` has\nno \"Operation not permitted\" line.\n\nGround rules: work only inside the current directory. Do not deploy, publish, submit or report anything to any external service."}],"source":"turn_start","userDisplayContent":null,"outcome":null}
