{"id":"assistant-cb2bc04a-83ff-59ec-8e41-5a68b3a2588e","sessionId":"16a6c158-5e2a-20ee-7ebb-60a1df0d404b","turnId":"turn-2f139b9a815d57e35b4d09c85f8e905f","inputEntryId":"user-turn-2f139b9a815d57e35b4d09c85f8e905f-1","createdAt":1794274327843,"updatedAt":1794274327843,"generationStatus":"completed","relatedEntryId":null,"type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The changes are complete. Let me provide a summary:\n\n## Summary\n\nI added a `codex-sandboxed` lane to `run.sh` that runs Codex CLI under the same sandbox profile as the `kimi` lane.\n\n**Changes to `run.sh`:**\n1. Updated the header comment to document the new lane\n2. Added `codex_sandboxed_run()` function that:\n   - Creates a scratch HOME (`/tmp/ch-XXXXXX`) and scratch output file (`/tmp/cout-XXXXXX`)\n   - Runs Codex under `sandbox-exec -f sandbox/agent.sb` with `-D HOME=<real home>`\n   - Directs Codex's `-o` output to the scratch file in `/tmp`\n   - After `sandbox-exec` returns, copies the scratch output to `$R/final.txt`\n   - Cleans up scratch resources and returns the exit code\n3. Added the `codex-sandboxed` case to the lane selector\n\n**Why the scratch output file:**\nThe colleague's note described exactly this problem: Codex's `-o` flag writes to a file, and when that path is under the denied real home folder, the write fails with \"Operation not permitted\" but Codex exits 0 anyway. The fix from the note applies directly: write to `/tmp` (allowed by the profile) and copy out after the sandbox exits. Stdout/stderr redirects still work because the shell opens them before `sandbox-exec` starts.\n\n**What applied from the note:**\n- The core problem and fix (write to `/tmp` scratch, copy out)\n- The observation about stdout/stderr working (opened before sandbox)\n- The verification advice\n\n**What didn't apply:**\n- Mistral Vibe's `--output-dir` flag (Codex uses `-o`)\n- Kimi-specific environment variables\n\nThe result is documented in `ANSWER.md`."}],"source":"harness","userDisplayContent":null,"outcome":{"type":"committed"}}
